What gitops 

	GitOps is a DevOps practice where Git is the single source of truth for infrastructure and application deployments.

	Instead of manually running commands on servers or Kubernetes clusters, you store everything in Git:

		Infrastructure configuration

		Kubernetes manifests

		Application deployment files

		Policies and automation scripts

	Then automation tools read Git and apply the changes to the system automatically.

--------------------------------------

Example (Real World)

Imagine you want to deploy a Python application to Kubernetes.

Traditional way:

	Developer → Build Docker image → Run kubectl apply manually

GitOps way:

Developer → Push YAML to Git → GitOps tool detects change → Deploys automatically

-----------------------------------------------------------------
Example 

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: python-app
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: python-app
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: python-app
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: python-app
        image: myrepo/python-app:v1

If you change:

replicas: 3 → replicas: 5

and push to Git, the GitOps tool automatically scales the application.

